  "id": "situational-differences",
  "term": "situational differences",
  "definition": "Situational differences are variations in the immediate social context or circumstances that can change how psychological factors are related. In this source, the term refers to differences within the same overall setting, such as being in a more relationship-fluid versus more stable interpersonal situation.",
